 ### [Mesh Culling via 3D Projection and Connected Components](6963-mesh-culling-via-3d-projection-and-connected-components.md)
-This method removes geometric artifacts and occluded regions from a 3D mesh by projecting its vertices into multiple camera views and comparing against reference depth maps. It classifies faces as "seen" (visible in at least 20 views), "unseen" (occluded or background), or "forecast" (distant potential geometry). It is distinct from neighbor-based culling (e.g., [Face Culling](8735-face-culling.md)) because it relies on multi-view consistency rather than local voxel occupancy, making it suitable for unbounded or non-volumetric meshes like those from Gaussian Splatting.
